body:
On the host, in the zsh config:

  za() { systemd-run --user --scope --collect --quiet zmx attach "$@" }
  _za() { (( CURRENT == 2 )) && compadd -- ${(f)"$(zmx list --short 2>/dev/null)"} }
  compdef _za za

So the launcher prefix, the idempotent create-or-attach, and completion over running sessions already exist and are in daily use. What `za` does not do is name or label: only bare names and flags pass through.

Consequence for scope: c-cgroup's 'birth' job is not zmux's contribution. Either zmux absorbs `za` (one code path that also writes labels) or zmux never creates and stays a reader. There is no third position worth the code.
